-- title:
--   Hecke sets meet only finitely many stabiliser cosets
-- statement:
--   Let $a,b\in\mathbb{Q}$ and let $\Lambda$ be a $\mathbb{Z}$-submodule of the quaternion algebra $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]$ which is an order in the sense of the predicate [`QuaternionAlgebra.IsOrder`](def/QuaternionAlgebra_Order.html#L11): $1\in\Lambda$, $\Lambda$ is closed under multiplication, the $\mathbb{Q}$-span of $\Lambda$ is all of $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]$, and $\Lambda$ is finitely generated over $\mathbb{Z}$. Write $\widehat{\Lambda}$ for [`Submodule.finiteAdeleBox`](def/Submodule_FiniteAdeleBox.html#L14) $\Lambda$, the additive subgroup of $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]\otimes_{\mathbb{Q}}\mathbb{A}_{\mathbb{Q},f}$ generated by the elements $z\otimes\alpha$ with $z\in\Lambda$ and $\alpha$ a finite adèle of $\mathbb{Q}$ all of whose components lie in the completed valuation rings, and write $U$ for [`Submodule.finiteIdeleStabilizer`](def/Submodule_FiniteAdeleBox.html#L26) $\Lambda$, the stabiliser of the set $\widehat{\Lambda}$ in the unit group $(\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]\otimes_{\mathbb{Q}}\mathbb{A}_{\mathbb{Q},f})^{\times}$. Let $\ell$ be a natural number (no primality or non-vanishing is assumed) and let $T$ be any subset of the units $h$ satisfying the four conditions defining [`QuaternionAlgebra.primeHeckeSet`](def/QuaternionAlgebra_ClassSetHecke.html#L109) $\Lambda$ $\ell$: $h\in\widehat{\Lambda}$, $\ell\cdot h^{-1}\in\widehat{\Lambda}$, $h^{-1}\notin\widehat{\Lambda}$ and $\ell^{-1}\cdot h\notin\widehat{\Lambda}$. Then the set of classes in the quotient group $(\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]\otimes_{\mathbb{Q}}\mathbb{A}_{\mathbb{Q},f})^{\times}/U$ that are the image of some element of $T$ is finite.
--
--   This is the adelic form of the classical finiteness of the double coset decomposition of a Hecke set for an order in a quaternion algebra: a Hecke set at $\ell$ is covered by finitely many cosets of the stabiliser of $\widehat{\Lambda}$. It supplies the coset-finiteness input for the Hecke correspondences on the class set and for the Čerednik–Drinfeld coset-graph comparisons with Eichler orders.
